 459. Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township. Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part. Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties. The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d01\", \"text\": \"from Wikimedia project Spanish Wikipedia located in the administrative territorial entity Crawford County 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia coordinate location 40°51'5 '' N, 82°49'22 '' W 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia population 1,234 statement is subject of 2020 United States Census determination method or standard census point in time 1 April 2020 1 reference stated in 2020 United States Census retrieved 1 January 2022 reference URL https : //data.census.gov/cedsci/table? t=Populations % 20and % 20People & g=0100000US, % 241600000 & y=2020 editor United States Census Bureau 1,234 determination method or\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"text\": \"Sandusky Township, Crawford County, Ohio Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States. As of the 2010 census the population was 1,234. Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township. Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part. Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties. The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d03\", \"text\": \"County , OH have `` super commutes '' in excess of 90 minutes . The chart below shows how the median household income in Sandusky County , OH compares to that of it 's neighboring and parent geographies . View Data Save Image Share / Embed Add Data to Cart View Data Save Image Share / Embed Add Data to Cart Car Ownership 2 cars Average Number The following chart displays the households in Sandusky County , OH distributed between a series of car ownership buckets compared to the national averages for each bucket . The largest share of households\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d04\", \"text\": \"41,228 and the median income for a family was $ 49,647 . Males had a median income of $ 40,304 versus $ 28,118 for females . The per capita income for the county was $ 20,590 . About 10.8 % of families and 13.0 % of the population were below the poverty line , including 21.3 % of those under age 18 and 6.2 % of those age 65 or over . [ 14 ] Politics [ edit ] Prior to 1924 , Crawford County was a strongly Democratic county . Since then , it has become strongly Republican ,\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"I do not have current or specific population data for Sandusky Township, Ohio.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"population of Sandusky Township, Ohio\", \"scope\": \"as of the 2010 census\", \"claim\": \"As of the 2010 census, the population of Sandusky Township, Ohio was 459.\", \"answer\": \"459\", \"quote\": \"As of the 2010 census the population was 459.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"population of Sandusky Township, Ohio\", \"scope\": \"as of 1 April 2020\", \"claim\": \"The population of Sandusky Township, Ohio was 1,234 as of 1 April 2020.\", \"answer\": \"1,234\", \"quote\": \"from Wikimedia project Spanish Wikipedia 